{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And your brother, etc., and it shall come to pass when, etc.</b> The interpretations of this are numerous. It may be said that he intended to say in this manner: all the blessings with which he blessed him shall hold <b>when</b> he serves his brother. And when he descends from this level — or it may intend the language of subjugation: when your subjugation shall be lost and destroyed, you shall break his yoke first, and afterward you shall descend, and the house of Jacob shall be fire, etc., and the house of Esau stubble (Obadiah 1:18), and it shall consume them. Therefore he was precise in saying <b>and it shall be</b> (והיה) — the language of joy, for then the heavens shall rejoice and the earth shall exult:" "<b>Or</b> it may intend: <b>and it shall come to pass when</b> you rule in the world, your supremacy over him will not endure, but rather ״you shall break his yoke from upon״ etc. — neither shall he rule over you nor shall you rule over him. And what he said immediately afterward, sins caused these."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:02.741479181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}